\title{Is the empty set a subset?}
\date{2026-02-18T13:07:49Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Recall the definition of the \em{empty set}:}

\transclude{006G}

\p{Question: is #{\varnothing \subseteq \N}?}

\p{Answer: yes! By definition, this means #{\all{a}{\varnothing} a \in \N}, so it really comes down to what we do with a #{\forall} whose domain is empty; but as we [discussed previously](004N), such a #{\forall} should be considered true.}

\p{In fact, the empty set is a subset of \em{every} set, even itself.}
